  "id": "panel-network",
  "after": "overview",
  "title": "A hiring panel is a small neural network.",
  "caption": "Candidate facts go in on the left. Each junior interviewer (a hidden neuron) mixes them, and the manager (the output neuron) makes the final call. Each line is a weight (वज़न, vazan): how much one neuron trusts the one before it. In a bigger network, a senior would be one more hidden layer.",
  "alt": "A network with three layers. Input layer: three circles for the candidate facts coding 8, interview 6 and experience 2. Hidden layer: three circles J1, J2 and J3 for junior interviewers, each joined by lines to all three inputs. Output layer: one circle M for the manager, joined to all three juniors, giving hire? 0.83. A note says each line is a weight, how much one neuron trusts the one before it, and that after a bad hire training changes every weight a little.",
